      "writtenOn": "2023-11-28T05:39:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unsure if I understand this comment correctly:\n\ncom.android.server.display.feature.DisplayManagerFlags:\nlog: \"No virtual method isDisplayOffloadEnabled()Z in class Lcom/android/server/display/feature/DisplayManagerFlags\" this method is called via HwBinder\n\nandroid.app.admin.flags.FeatureFlagsImpl:\nlog: \"No pending exception expected: java.lang.NoSuchFieldError: no \"J\" field \"mPtr\" in class \"Lcom/android/server/input/NativeInputManagerService$NativeImpl;\" this is caused by some obfuscation for native implementation in jni (com_android_server_input_InputManagerService)\n\nFor com.android.server.ThreadPriorityBooster, it\u0027s methods are referenced in services.jar \"java.lang.NoSuchMethodError: No direct method \u003cinit\u003e(II)V in class Lcom/android/server/ThreadPriorityBooster; or its super classes (declaration of \u0027com.android.server.ThreadPriorityBooster\u0027 appears in /system/framework/services.jar)\"\n\nI added these rules to cover exceptions during boottime, and I agree that there are rooms for a generic solutions and optimizations done to these rules. Let\u0027s file a bug to keep track of the work.",
