      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T18:52:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s super helpful, thanks!\n\n@tyiu@google.com I guess this highlights that we don\u0027t really have anything in presubmit with this config enabled, so it could be pretty fragile. Unless there\u0027s a setting that makes ART a bit less strict about missing dex classes/methods that ae present in the dexpreopt profile. @jiakaiz@google.com may know.\n\nAll that said, I think this probably highlights a broader issues, which is that the system server profiles are generated with the default mode (SYSTEM_OPTIMIZE_JAVA \u003d shrinking), and it\u0027s not clear how much the corresponding profile could/should look like with FULL_SYSTEM_OPTIMIZE_JAVA (shrinking + optimization). Inlining and class merging can definitely change the nature of the generated profiles.",
      "parentUuid": "996869a8_be16a301",
      "revId": "d5dd07ced9e823a231ebe5755773caee4a87c17f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
